# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in the key. It is read only by
# the Vite dev/preview server (see vite.config.ts), which proxies /api/henrik/*
# to the HenrikDev API with the key attached. `vite build` never reads it, so
# the key is never part of the built site.
#
# Get a free Basic key: https://api.henrikdev.xyz/dashboard/ -> API Keys -> Generate New Key
HENRIKDEV_API_KEY=

# Optional: point the local proxy at a different upstream (e.g. a mock server).
# HENRIKDEV_API_BASE=https://api.henrikdev.xyz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRODUCTION (Cloudflare Pages)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Do NOT use this file. Set the same variable on the Cloudflare project instead:
#   Workers & Pages -> <project> -> Settings -> Variables and Secrets -> Add
#     Type: Secret, Name: HENRIKDEV_API_KEY, Environment: Production (and Preview if wanted)
# or with Wrangler:
#   npx wrangler pages secret put HENRIKDEV_API_KEY --project-name <project>
# Then redeploy. The Pages Function in functions/api/henrik reads it at runtime.
